(SLO Handbook - FS100) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(Owner: SRE. Applies to: the chat, upload and login journeys of FS100. Last reviewed:) '
(2026-10.) '
() '
/F1 14 Tf
(1. Why service level objectives) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(A service level objective \(SLO\) is a target for how reliable a user journey must be,) '
(measured over a rolling window. It turns "is the system good enough?" into a number that) '
(engineering and product agree on. Reliability above the target is not a goal in itself:) '
(every extra nine costs effort that could go into features.) '
() '
/F1 14 Tf
(2. Service level indicators) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(A service level indicator \(SLI\) is the measured ratio of good events to all events.) '
(FS100 uses three SLIs:) '
(- Chat availability: share of chat requests that end with a done event instead of an) '
(error event or a timeout.) '
(- Chat latency: share of chat requests whose first token arrives within 3 seconds.) '
(- Upload success: share of uploaded documents that reach the status ready within 5) '
(minutes.) '
(SLIs are measured at the NestJS API, as close to the user as possible, not inside the AI) '
(service.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
