/F1 14 Tf
(3. Targets) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(All targets use a rolling 28-day window.) '
(- Chat availability: 99.5 percent.) '
(- Chat latency \(first token within 3 seconds\): 95 percent.) '
(- Upload success: 99 percent.) '
(- Login availability: inherited from Keycloak, 99.9 percent.) '
() '
/F1 14 Tf
(4. Error budget) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(The error budget is the allowed amount of unreliability: 100 percent minus the target.) '
(For chat availability that is 0.5 percent of all chat requests in 28 days, or roughly 3) '
(hours and 22 minutes of full outage.) '
() '
/F1 14 Tf
(5. Error budget policy) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(- While budget remains, releases ship normally.) '
(- When more than 50 percent of the budget is consumed in the first half of the window,) '
(risky changes need a second reviewer.) '
(- When the budget is exhausted, feature releases stop. Only fixes for reliability and) '
(security ship until the SLI is back above target for 7 days.) '
(- A single incident that consumes more than 20 percent of the budget requires a) '
(postmortem, even if it was a SEV3.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
