(6. Alerting on burn rate) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(Alerts fire on the burn rate: how fast the error budget is consumed relative to the) '
(target. A burn rate of 1 uses exactly the whole budget in 28 days.) '
(Multi-window alerts avoid both slow detection and flapping:) '
(- Page: burn rate above 14.4 over the last hour and over the last 5 minutes \(2 percent) '
(of the budget in one hour\).) '
(- Page: burn rate above 6 over the last 6 hours and over the last 30 minutes \(5 percent) '
(of the budget in 6 hours\).) '
(- Ticket: burn rate above 1 over the last 3 days.) '
(The short window makes the alert stop quickly once the problem is fixed.) '
() '
/F1 14 Tf
(7. Review cadence) '
/F1 11 Tf
() '
(SLOs are reviewed every quarter with product. Questions for the review: did users) '
(complain while the SLO was met \(target too loose\)? Did we burn budget on events users) '
(did not notice \(SLI measures the wrong thing\)? Changes to targets are recorded in the) '
(changelog of this handbook.) '
ET
endstream
